---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import Measure from "../components/Measure.astro";
import Quote from "../components/Quote.astro";
import { latestRelease } from "../lib/release";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const release = latestRelease();
---

<Page
  title="Install iyi"
  summary="Install iyi with one command: the latest release into ~/.local, on Linux x86-64 or macOS arm64, then run hello. Or unpack the tarball by hand, or build from source."
>
  <section class="wrap head">
    <p class="label">Install, <a href={`${base}changelog/`}>version {release.version}</a></p>
    <h1>One command, then hello.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The installer is a POSIX shell script over <code>curl</code> and{" "}
      <code>tar</code>. It picks the release for your machine, unpacks it into{" "}
      <code>~/.local</code>, and checks that the binary starts. The second line
      runs the first sample it shipped with.
    </p>
    <Quote id="install" as="console" caption="install, then run hello" copy />
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h2>What it does</h2>
        <ul class="points">
          <li>
            <strong>Picks the tarball for <code>uname</code>:</strong>{" "}
            <code>linux-x86_64</code> or <code>darwin-arm64</code>. Anything
            else is refused by name, with a pointer to building from source.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Follows the latest release</strong> on GitHub, without the
            API; today that is {release.version}, from {release.date}.{" "}
            <code>IYI_VERSION={release.version}</code> pins one.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Unpacks into <code>~/.local</code>.</strong>{" "}
            <code>IYI_PREFIX</code> moves it; the tarball is relocatable.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Nothing to configure.</strong> <code>bin/iyi</code> finds
            its libraries beside itself. No <code>IYI_PATH</code>, no LLVM to
            install: LLVM is inside the binary.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>What you get</h2>
        <ul class="points">
          <li>
            <strong>The compiler</strong>, and the same binary under Crystal's
            name for <code>.cr</code> files.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Both libraries:</strong> iyi's own,{" "}
            <Measure of="prelude_kb" unit="KB" /> on disk, and Crystal's
            standard library for <code>iyi build --crystal</code>, so your
            shards work from the first minute.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The samples</strong> under <code>share/iyi/samples</code>,
            the programs the <a href={`${base}learn/`}>lessons</a> are built on.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The tools:</strong> <code>iyi check</code>, <code>fix</code>,{" "}
            <code>test</code>, <code>doc</code>, <code>mod</code>,{" "}
            <code>lsp</code> and <code>mcp</code>, all one binary.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>By hand</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      The installer does two things you can do yourself. Download the tarball
      for your machine from the{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/sdogruyol/iyi/releases/latest">latest release</a>,
      then:
    </p>
    <Quote id="install_manual" as="console" caption="the same two lines, by hand" copy />
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>From source</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Other platforms, or the current tree rather than a release: clone the
      repository and <code>make</code>. It needs a Crystal compiler to
      bootstrap from and LLVM; the README's{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/sdogruyol/iyi#getting-it">Getting it</a>{" "}
      section names the versions and every command.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap next">
    <h2>Then</h2>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a class="cta" href={`${base}playground/`}>Take the tour</a>
      <a class="cta ghost" href={`${base}learn/`}>Learn the rule</a>
      <a class="cta ghost" href={`${base}#crystal`}>Coming from Crystal</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    section {
      padding-block: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    }

    .head {
      padding-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    }

    .head h1 {
      font-size: var(--step-4);
      margin-block: 0.5rem 0.8rem;
    }

    .lede {
      color: var(--graphite);
      max-width: 60ch;
      font-size: var(--step-0);
      margin-block-end: 1.4rem;
    }

    .head :global(.console) {
      max-width: 60rem;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: var(--step-2);
      margin-block-end: 0.6rem;
    }

    .sub {
      color: var(--graphite);
      max-width: 62ch;
      margin-block-end: 1rem;
    }

    .cols {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 22rem), 1fr));
      gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    }

    .points {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.8rem;
    }

    .points li {
      position: relative;
      padding-inline-start: 1.6rem;
      color: var(--graphite);
    }

    .points li::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      left: 0.1rem;
      top: 0.55em;
      width: 0.5rem;
      height: 0.5rem;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--brand);
    }

    .points strong {
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .next {
      padding-block-end: 3rem;
    }

    .hero-cta {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0.8rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
  </style>
</Page>
